From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:12:38 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: hi846: Report the pixel rate the timing runs at
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The pixel rate is worked out from the current mode's link frequency, so
a binned mode on a slower link reports a slower rate. Its line and frame
lengths stay those of the full readout, though: all modes have lines of
3800 pixels, and 2526 lines at 30 fps, 842 at 90 fps or 631 at 120 fps,
which all give 288 MHz from a 24 MHz clock, the full readout's rate. On
four lanes the 1632x1224 mode measures 30 fps with frame lengths of
2526 lines, where its 180 MHz link implies a pixel rate of 144 MHz and
15 fps.

The control is also created with the rate of the default 640x480 mode,
72 MHz on four lanes, as its maximum, so the rates of the faster modes
are clamped to it. Userspace that works out the line duration from the
pixel rate, as libcamera does, gets lines four times too long:
libcamera reported exposures of 133 ms at 30 fps.

Report the full readout's rate in every mode.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c | 20 +++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
index 7ad691364..5bec2105d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
@@ -1157,9 +1157,8 @@ static const struct hi846_mode supported_modes[] = {
 		.height = 480,
 		.mipi_clk_div_2lane = 4,
 		/*
-		 * Dummy but necessary if we set this mode default, otherwise
-		 * hi846_calc_pixel_rate() will be broken in
-		 * hi846_init_controls()
+		 * Dummy but necessary, as the probe works out every mode's
+		 * link frequency
 		 */
 		.mipi_clk_div_4lane = 8,
 		.fps = 120,
@@ -1381,14 +1380,17 @@ static int hi846_get_link_freq_index(const struct hi846 *hi846,
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The line and frame lengths of every mode give its frame rate at one pixel
+ * rate, that of the full readout over four lanes: 288 MHz from a 24 MHz clock,
+ * for lines of 3800 and 2526 lines at 30 fps, 842 at 90 fps and 631 at 120 fps.
+ * The binned modes send fewer pixels on a slower link, but their timing does
+ * not change with it.
+ */
 static u64 hi846_calc_pixel_rate(struct hi846 *hi846)
 {
-	u64 link_freq = hi846_get_link_freq(hi846, hi846->cur_mode);
-	u64 pixel_rate = link_freq * 2 * hi846->nr_lanes;
-
-	do_div(pixel_rate, HI846_RGB_DEPTH);
-
-	return pixel_rate;
+	return mul_u64_u32_div(clk_get_rate(hi846->clock), 90 * 2 * 4,
+			       3 * 2 * HI846_RGB_DEPTH);
 }
 
 static int hi846_read_reg(struct hi846 *hi846, u16 reg, u8 *val)
